
  IOAM GOB v3 kernel (Linux 6.18-rc1), running in your browser: QEMU
  compiled to WebAssembly, one CPU, everything in memory.

  1. The live dashboard (about 40 s to start):
       gob-demo-5node-recv-tmux.sh && tmux attach -t gobdemo
     then type in the CONTROL pane:
       gob-encap combined ; gob-ping 10   RECEIVED fills during the ping
       gob-metric set n3 70 ; gob-ping    the change reaches n4 and n5
       gob-help                           all the commands
     Ctrl-b d leaves tmux, Ctrl-b R refreshes the panes.

  2. The automatic check (about one minute):
       gob-demo-5node-recv-auto.sh

  3. Build the eBPF program with clang (about 90 s), then run 1 or 2
     again to load your build (vi is there to edit it):
       cd /opt/gob/src && make
     bpf_printk output: bpftool prog tracelog

  Topology: h1 - n1 - n2 - n3 - n4 - n5 - h2. n1 encapsulates, n5
  decapsulates. Reloading the page starts from scratch.

